  "title": "Coordination Number Basics",
  "questions": [
    {
      "question": "Coordination number counts:",
      "options": [
        "Electrons in metal",
        "σ-donor atoms bonded to metal",
        "Ligand mass",
        "Oxidation state only"
      ],
      "correct_answer": "σ-donor atoms bonded to metal",
      "explanation": "CN = donor atoms directly bonded."
    },
    {
      "question": "[Fe(CN)6]4- has coordination number:",
      "options": [
        "4",
        "6",
        "8",
        "2"
      ],
      "correct_answer": "6",
      "explanation": "Six cyanide ligands → CN=6."
    },
    {
      "question": "Coordination entity contains:",
      "options": [
        "Central metal ion + ligands",
        "Only anions",
        "Only cations",
        "Free solvent"
      ],
      "correct_answer": "Central metal ion + ligands",
      "explanation": "Complex = metal + attached ligands."
    }
  ]
}

system_prompt:
{{ studio_system_prompt }}

USER/TASK TEMPLATE:
Expert quiz author for Class 11–12 self-assessment (incl. JEE/NEET/board prep). Create a quiz from the provided material.

**Selected sources:** {{ selected_source_count }} document(s).

SCOPE: source content excerpt only (or chat conversation if explicitly requested) — questions/options/explanations must be supported by it.
{% if selected_source_count | int > 1 %}
Multi-source: distribute across all represented sources. Related sources → may blend naturally; unrelated → keep each question scoped to one source (don't force together unrelated facts — that tests memorizing an arbitrary pairing, not understanding).
{% endif %}

OUTPUT (strict): ONE valid JSON object only, no markdown/fences/extra text: `{"title":"...","questions":[{"question":"...","options":["A","B","C","D"],"correct_answer":"exact option string","explanation":"1-2 sentences"}]}`

{% if custom_instructions and custom_instructions.strip() %}
COUNT: per Additional instructions below (overrides default).
{% else %}
COUNT: 5–7 questions; if source is thin, as many solid ones as it supports (min 3 if possible).
{% endif %}

QUALITY: exactly 4 options/question; test understanding not memorization; unambiguous wording; no duplicate questions/near-duplicate options; concise source-accurate explanations.

SINGLE-CORRECTNESS (mandatory, per question before finalizing): exactly one option defensibly correct — check the other three for any reasonable alternate reading that could make them also-correct; revise if so. Never ship two viable answers. `correct_answer` matches one option verbatim.

DISTRACTORS: build from plausible exam-realistic errors (common misconception, near-miss calculation/sign/unit error, related-but-distinct term mix-up, value from a different scenario in the source) — not eliminable by guessing alone.

NUMERIC/FORMULA INTEGRITY: verify sign, unit, exponent on every formula/number before finalizing — the highest-cost mistake here, since a wrong number gets memorized as fact.

SELF-VERIFICATION (internal): is `correct_answer` actually supported by the excerpt, are all 3 distractors genuinely wrong per it, does the explanation reflect the source (not general knowledge)? Fix silently before output.

CUSTOM INSTRUCTIONS: honor requested difficulty (reasoning depth, distractors, vocabulary); topic focus → most questions relate to it; "full breadth"/"all sources" → distribute across retrieved material.

{% if retrieval_queries_note and retrieval_queries_note.strip() %}
Retrieval queries: {{ retrieval_queries_note }}
{% endif %}
{% if context and context.strip() %}
Source content:
{{ context }}
{% else %}
No source content. Return exactly: {"title": "Insufficient source text", "questions": []}. No general-knowledge questions.
{% endif %}

{% if custom_instructions %}
Additional instructions: {{ custom_instructions }}
{% endif %}

gold_json:
{"quiz_json": "{
  "title": "Independent Events Quiz",
  "questions": [
    {
      "question": "For independent A and B, P(A∩B) equals:",
      "options": [
        "P(A)+P(B)",
        "P(A)P(B)",
        "P(A)/P(B)",
        "1"
      ],
      "correct_answer": "P(A)P(B)",
      "explanation": "Independence: multiply probabilities."
    },
    {
      "question": "Classical P(E) equals:",
      "options": [
        "favourable/total outcomes",
        "total/favourable",
        "P(A)+P(B)",
        "Always 1/2"
      ],
      "correct_answer": "favourable/total outcomes",
      "explanation": "Laplace definition."
    },
    {
      "question": "P(A∪B) general addition rule:",
      "options": [
        "P(A)+P(B)-P(A∩B)",
        "P(A)P(B)",
        "P(A)-P(B)",
        "P(A)/P(B)"
      ],
      "correct_answer": "P(A)+P(B)-P(A∩B)",
      "explanation": "Inclusion-exclusion."
    },
    {
      "question": "If A and B independent, knowing B occurred:",
      "options": [
        "Changes P(A)",
        "Does not change P(A)",
        "Makes P(A)=0",
        "Makes P(A)=1"
      ],
      "correct_answer": "Does not change P(A)",
      "explanation": "Independence means no influence."
    },
    {
      "question": "Bayes theorem relates:",
      "options": [
        "Prior and likelihood to posterior",
        "Only means",
        "Only variances",
        "Matrix rank"
      ],
      "correct_answer": "Prior and likelihood to posterior",
      "explanation": "Bayes updates beliefs with evidence."
    }
  ]
}"}

