      "slide_number": 2,
      "title": "Precise Pairing: A-T and G-C Rules",
      "bullets": [
        "Within the DNA double helix, bases pair specifically across the two strands.",
        "**Adenine (A)** always pairs with **Thymine (T)**.",
        "**Guanine (G)** always pairs with **Cytosine (C)**.",
        "This **complementary pairing** is fundamental to DNA's function."
      ]
    },
    {
      "slide_number": 3,
      "title": "Copying the Code: Semiconservative Replication",
      "bullets": [
        "When a cell divides, its DNA must be accurately copied through **replication**.",
        "DNA replication is **semiconservative** â each new DNA molecule consists of one original strand and one newly synthesized strand.",
        "This mechanism ensures genetic information is faithfully passed to daughter cells."
      ]
    },
    {
      "slide_number": 4,
      "title": "From DNA to Protein: The Role of mRNA",
