{"slide_deck_markdown": "[
    {
        "slide_number": 1,
        "title": "The Blueprint of Life: DNA's Double Helix",
        "bullets": [
            "DNA, the molecule of inheritance, forms a **double helix** structure.",
            "It's composed of two strands wound around each other, like a twisted ladder.",
            "The 'rungs' of this ladder are made of **nucleotide base pairs**."
        ]
    },
    {
        "slide_number": 2,
        "title": "Specific Pairing: A-T and G-C Rules",
        "bullets": [
            "DNA's stability comes from specific base pairing rules.",
            "**Adenine (A)** always pairs with **Thymine (T)**.",
            "**Guanine (G)** always pairs with **Cytosine (C)**.",
            "This precise pairing ensures accurate genetic information transfer."
        ]
    },
    {
        "slide_number": 3,
        "title": "Semiconservative Replication: Copying the Code",
        "bullets": [
            "When a cell divides, DNA must be accurately copied through **semiconservative replication**.",
            "The double helix unwinds, and each original strand serves as a **template**.",
            "New complementary strands are synthesized, resulting in two new DNA molecules.",
            "Each new DNA molecule contains **one original and one newly synthesized strand**."
        ]
    },
    {
        "slide_number": 4,
        "title": "From DNA to Protein: The Role of mRNA",
        "bullets": [
            "DNA's genetic instructions are carried out by **messenger RNA (mRNA)**.",
            "mRNA is a single-stranded molecule that copies specific gene sequences from DNA.",
            "It acts as an **intermediate messenger**, transporting the genetic code from the nucleus to ribosomes.",
            "What would happen if mRNA couldn't accurately copy the DNA sequence?"
        ]
    },
    {
        "slide_number": 5,
        "title": "Conclusion: The Central Dogma of Molecular Inheritance",
        "bullets": [
            "DNA's **double helix** and **specific base pairing (A-T, G-C)** are fundamental to life.",
            "**Semiconservative replication** ensures faithful copying of genetic material for new cells.",
            "**mRNA** is the crucial link, carrying DNA's instructions to ribosomes for **protein synthesis**.",
            "This precise molecular machinery underpins all biological inheritance and function."
        ]
    }
]"}

