        "slide_number": 2,
        "title": "Oral Cavity: Salivary Amylase Initiates Starch Digestion",
        "bullets": [
            "The mouth is where chemical digestion **begins**.",
            "**Salivary amylase** (ptyalin) is secreted by salivary glands.",
            "It acts on **complex carbohydrates** (starch), breaking them into smaller dextrins and disaccharides.",
            "Optimal pH for salivary amylase is around **6.7-7.0**."
        ]
    },
